# Execute a test in all endpoints
pytest tests/foreman/{cli,api,ui}/test_host.py

# subset by name fragment
-k negative

# multithread
-n 4

# run last failed, run last failed first
-lf
-ff

# To run a specific test within a module:

pytest test_mod.py::test_func

# Another example specifying a test method in the command line:

pytest test_mod.py::TestClass::test_method

pytest gathers tests according to a naming convention. By default any file that is to contain tests must be named starting with test_, classes that hold tests must be named starting with Test, and any function in a file that should be treated as a test must also start with test_. 

# scopes of @pytest.fixture(scope="")

function -- before every function (like setUp, use yield to tearDown)
class    -- before every class (like setUpClass, yield to tearDownClass)
module   -- runs per module
package  -- runs per package
session  -- per session, use conftest.py file (will be available to tests within the same dir)
